IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `la-dates`
IMPORT `la-rules`

-- Limitation Act 2005 (WA) -- the questions of the CLAIMANT.
--
-- SEAT: the individual to whom a cause of action accrues and who brings, or proposes to bring, the action -- the injured
-- person, the worker with a dust disease, the survivor of child sexual abuse, the family member suing for a death, the
-- party to a contract or deed: "When did my claim accrue?", "By when must I start my action?", "Can I still start it on
-- this day?", "Can the court give me more time, and to when?", "Did the other side's acknowledgment or payment give me
-- more time?", "Can I sue now for abuse that was barred or settled before 1 July 2018?". One question (s 81) is asked by
-- the same individual when answering a claim with a counterclaim. The court, the defendant's insurer and the Minister get
-- no seat: the court's satisfaction and leave are asked as facts.
--
-- Every question takes plain facts (yes/no, dates, numbers, a choice from a list) and calls the rules of la-rules.l4. The
-- time bar is a DEONTIC rule run inside `Can I still commence my action on this day`; no question takes a DEONTIC or an
-- EVENT.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website at 2026-09-07: "Limitation Act 2005", State of Western
-- Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). See SOURCE-LICENSE.md.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Limitation Act 2005: the claimant's questions`

§§ `When my claim accrued (personal injury and dust disease)`

@export When did my cause of action for damages for a personal injury accrue, so that my limitation period started (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 55, 56, 57)? Ordinarily when you became aware of a not insignificant injury or its first sign appeared, whichever was earlier; for an asbestos or silica dust injury, when you had knowledge of the relevant facts; if the person died first, at the death.
GIVEN `is it from dust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is attributable to breathing in asbestos or silica dust
      `did I become aware` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have become aware that you sustained a personal injury that is not insignificant (for a dust injury, answer no)
      `day I became aware` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware of it (any date if you have not)
      `did a first sign appear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a first symptom, clinical sign or other manifestation of an injury that is not insignificant has appeared (for a dust injury, answer no)
      `day of the first sign` IS A DATE @desc The day the first symptom, clinical sign or other manifestation appeared (any date if none)
      `did I know before 1984` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dust injury: whether you already had knowledge of the relevant facts (significant injury, its cause, who to sue) before 1 January 1984
      `do I know the relevant facts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a dust injury: whether you now have knowledge of the relevant facts (see the knowledge question: a significant injury, caused by the act or omission, the identity of the defendant)
      `day I gained that knowledge` IS A DATE @desc For a dust injury: the day you first had that knowledge (any date if you do not)
      `did the person die of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person has died as a result of the injury (answer for them if you are the family or estate)
      `day of the death` IS A DATE @desc The day of the death (any date if none)
GIVETH AN `Accrual`
`When did my personal injury claim accrue` MEANS
    `ss 55-57 -- when the cause of action accrued` `is it from dust` `did I become aware` `day I became aware` `did a first sign appear` `day of the first sign` `did I know before 1984` `do I know the relevant facts` `day I gained that knowledge` `did the person die of it` `day of the death`

@export For an asbestos or silica dust injury, is my injury "significant", so that my claim can accrue (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 56(3), (4))? It must be serious enough to justify suing a defendant who admits liability and can pay; a workers' compensation injury also needs the parties' agreement or a medical panel finding of at least 30% disability (1981 Act s 93D(2)) or 25% whole of person impairment.
GIVEN `is it serious enough to sue for` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you would reasonably have considered the injury serious enough to justify suing a defendant who did not dispute liability and could pay a judgment
      `is it a workers compensation injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is a disability or injury from employment under the workers' compensation Acts (the Workers' Compensation and Injury Management Act 1981, or the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 Part 7 Division 2 from its commencement)
      `did the parties agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the person you would sue have agreed that the injury is significant
      `which panel finding` IS A `Medical panel finding` @desc The medical panel finding you have, if any: none; a 1981 Act medical panel degree of disability (s 93D(2)); a 1981 Act medical panel whole of person impairment (ss 146A, 146C, on or after 14 November 2005); or a Dust Disease Medical Panel permanent whole of person impairment (2023 Act)
      `what percentage` IS A NUMBER @desc The percentage the panel found (for example 25 for 25%; 0 if none)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my dust injury significant` MEANS
    `s 56(3), (4) -- the dust injury is significant` `is it serious enough to sue for` `is it a workers compensation injury` `did the parties agree` `which panel finding` `what percentage`

@export For an asbestos or silica dust injury, do I have "knowledge of the relevant facts", which starts my limitation period (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 56(2), (5))? You need to know the injury is significant, that it was caused by the act or omission you sue for, who the defendant is, and, if someone else did it, who and why the defendant answers for it. Knowledge includes what you could reasonably have found out, with reasonable medical or expert advice.
GIVEN `is the injury significant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is significant (the answer to the significance question)
      `do I know it was caused by it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know (or could reasonably have found out) that the injury was caused, wholly or partly, by the act or omission you say gives you the claim
      `do I know who to sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you know (or could reasonably have found out) who the defendant is
      `was it someone else's act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you say the act or omission was that of someone other than the defendant (for example an employee of the defendant)
      `do I know who and why` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether you know who that person was and the further facts that make the defendant answerable (answer yes if not applicable)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Do I have knowledge of the relevant facts` MEANS
    `s 56(2) -- I have knowledge of the relevant facts` `is the injury significant` `do I know it was caused by it` `do I know who to sue` `was it someone else's act` `do I know who and why`

§§ `Child sexual abuse (no limitation period)`

@export Is my claim a child sexual abuse action, for which no limitation period applies at all, however long ago the abuse happened (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 6A, 90)? The court can still stop a case where a fair trial is no longer possible.
GIVEN `did it result from sexual abuse of me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your personal injury results, directly or indirectly, from an act or omission towards you that was sexual abuse
      `was I under 18 then` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were under 18 when the abuse happened
      `is it only a death or estate claim` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim could be brought only because of the Fatal Accidents Act 1959 (a family's claim for a death) or the Law Reform (Miscellaneous Provisions) Act 1941 (a claim surviving to an estate); answer no if it is your own claim
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my claim a child sexual abuse action` MEANS
    `s 6A(1), (6) -- it is a child sexual abuse action` `did it result from sexual abuse of me` `was I under 18 then` `is it only a death or estate claim`

@export My child sexual abuse claim was statute barred, or settled, before 1 July 2018: can I sue now (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 89 to 92)? A barred claim may be brought despite the bar or an earlier dismissal; a claim settled after it was barred needs the court's leave, which can set the settlement aside.
GIVEN `is it a child sexual abuse action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim is a child sexual abuse action (the answer to that question)
      `was it barred before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, just before 1 July 2018, the claim could not be brought because a limitation period had expired (or an old Crown Suits Act or Limitation Act 1935 time bar applied)
      `was it settled before 1 July 2018` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you settled the claim before 1 July 2018
      `was it barred when settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you settled it: whether the claim was already statute barred when you settled
GIVETH A `Where Part 7 leaves my claim`
`Can I sue now on my barred or settled abuse claim` MEANS
    `ss 89-92 -- where Part 7 leaves my claim` `is it a child sexual abuse action` `was it barred before 1 July 2018` `was it settled before 1 July 2018` `was it barred when settled`

@export Can this court set aside the earlier judgment or dismissal of my child sexual abuse claim on the ground it was statute barred (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 91(2), (3), (6))? Only if it is satisfied that it is just and reasonable; a court other than the Supreme Court cannot set aside another court's judgment.
GIVEN `is it the Supreme Court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are applying to the Supreme Court of Western Australia
      `was it this court's judgment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the earlier judgment or dismissal was given by the same court you are applying to
      `is the court satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that it is just and reasonable to set it aside (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can this court set aside the earlier judgment` MEANS
    `s 91(3), (6) -- the court may set aside the earlier judgment` `is it the Supreme Court` `was it this court's judgment` `is the court satisfied`

@export How much of what I was paid under my earlier settlement is taken to relate to the child sexual abuse, which the court may take into account (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 92(6), (7))? Half, where the settlement also covered other things and did not say how much was for the abuse.
GIVEN `how much was paid` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount paid to you under the settlement agreement, in dollars
      `was it only about the abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement related only to that child sexual abuse
      `did it say the share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement expressly said how far it, and the amounts paid, related to that child sexual abuse
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`How much of my settlement relates to the abuse` MEANS
    `s 92(7) -- the amount taken to relate to the abuse` `how much was paid` `was it only about the abuse` `did it say the share`

§§ `My time limit`

@export By when must I start my court action, or is there no time limit (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 4, 6A, 6B, 13 to 18, 30 to 36, 52, 53)? Personal injury, a death claim and trespass to the person: 3 years; contribution: 2; deed: 12; most others: 6. Longer if you were under 18 or have a mental disability; none for child sexual abuse or a subsequent dust disease. Claims that accrued before 15 November 2005 follow the old law. A time limit in another Act (for example workers' compensation) prevails (s 9).
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for: damages for a personal injury (including disease); a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 claim for a death; trespass to the person, assault, battery or false imprisonment; contribution from another wrongdoer; an action on a deed; any other cause of action (for example a contract); or land, mortgage, defamation, account, equitable, tax or arbitration claims (not answered)
      `is it child sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a child sexual abuse action (the answer to that question)
      `is it a subsequent dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a subsequent action for subsequent damages for a subsequent dust disease, as the Civil Liability Act 2002 Part 2 Division 5 defines them (a second claim after provisional damages)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued (for personal injury, the answer to the accrual question; for a Fatal Accidents Act claim, the day of the death; for contribution, the day of the judgment, award or settlement fixing your liability)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (the person to whom the cause of action accrued)
      `did it come to me on a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim came to you on the death of a person who died under 18, or with a mental disability (then your own age or disability gives no further time)
      `days without a guardian under 18` IS A NUMBER @desc If you were under 18 when it accrued: the number of days after it accrued, and before you turned 18, during which you had no guardian (no one with legal responsibility for your long-term care who could practicably sue for you); 0 if none
      `close relationship under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were under 18 when it accrued: whether, at any time before you turned 18, the person you would sue (or someone they are vicariously liable for) was in a close relationship with you: a parent or carer with legal responsibility for you, or someone it was reasonable not to sue, or about whom it was reasonable not to tell
      `have I had a mental disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time since it accrued you have had a mental disability (an intellectual disability, psychiatric condition, acquired brain injury or dementia that left you unable to make reasonable judgments about yourself or your property)
      `days I had no guardian while disabled` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the number of days during the disability in which you had no guardian or administrator able to consider suing for you; 0 if none
      `close relationship during disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether during the disability the person you would sue was your guardian, or someone it was reasonable not to sue, or about whom it was reasonable not to tell
      `has that relationship ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether that relationship has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day that relationship ended (any date if it has not, or there was none)
GIVETH A `Time limit`
`By when must I commence my action` MEANS
    `the time limit for` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                                IS `what kind of action`
        `claim is a child sexual abuse action`      IS `is it child sexual abuse`
        `claim is a subsequent dust disease action` IS `is it a subsequent dust disease action`
        `claim accrual day`                         IS `day it accrued`
        `claimant birth day`                        IS `my date of birth`
        `claim came on the death of a minor or disabled person` IS `did it come to me on a death`
        `days without a guardian while under 18`    IS `days without a guardian under 18`
        `close relationship while under 18`         IS `close relationship under 18`
        `mental disability after accrual`           IS `have I had a mental disability`
        `days without a guardian while disabled`    IS `days I had no guardian while disabled`
        `close relationship while disabled`         IS `close relationship during disability`
        `close relationship has ceased`             IS `has that relationship ended`
        `close relationship ceased on`              IS `day it ended`)

@export Can I still start my court action on this day, or has my limitation period run out (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 12 to 18, 30 to 36)? An action starts when the writ or other originating application is issued. If the time has run, ask whether the court can extend it, or whether a confirmation gave you more time.
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for: damages for a personal injury (including disease); a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 claim for a death; trespass to the person, assault, battery or false imprisonment; contribution from another wrongdoer; an action on a deed; any other cause of action (for example a contract); or land, mortgage, defamation, account, equitable, tax or arbitration claims (not answered)
      `is it child sexual abuse` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a child sexual abuse action (the answer to that question)
      `is it a subsequent dust disease action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a subsequent action for subsequent damages for a subsequent dust disease, as the Civil Liability Act 2002 Part 2 Division 5 defines them
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued (for personal injury, the answer to the accrual question; for a Fatal Accidents Act claim, the day of the death)
      `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth (the person to whom the cause of action accrued)
      `did it come to me on a death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the claim came to you on the death of a person who died under 18, or with a mental disability
      `days without a guardian under 18` IS A NUMBER @desc If you were under 18 when it accrued: the days after it accrued, and before you turned 18, during which you had no guardian; 0 if none
      `close relationship under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were under 18 when it accrued: whether before you turned 18 the person you would sue was in a close relationship with you (a parent or carer, or someone it was reasonable not to sue or not to tell about)
      `have I had a mental disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time since it accrued you have had a mental disability that left you unable to make reasonable judgments about yourself or your property
      `days I had no guardian while disabled` IS A NUMBER @desc If so: the days during the disability in which you had no guardian or administrator able to consider suing for you; 0 if none
      `close relationship during disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether during the disability the person you would sue was your guardian, or someone it was reasonable not to sue or not to tell about
      `has that relationship ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If so: whether that relationship has ended
      `day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day that relationship ended (any date if it has not)
      `day I would commence` IS A DATE @desc The day the writ or other originating application would be (or was) issued by the court
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I still commence my action on this day` MEANS
    `the action can be commenced on` `day I would commence` `for` (`The claim` WITH
        `claim kind`                                IS `what kind of action`
        `claim is a child sexual abuse action`      IS `is it child sexual abuse`
        `claim is a subsequent dust disease action` IS `is it a subsequent dust disease action`
        `claim accrual day`                         IS `day it accrued`
        `claimant birth day`                        IS `my date of birth`
        `claim came on the death of a minor or disabled person` IS `did it come to me on a death`
        `days without a guardian while under 18`    IS `days without a guardian under 18`
        `close relationship while under 18`         IS `close relationship under 18`
        `mental disability after accrual`           IS `have I had a mental disability`
        `days without a guardian while disabled`    IS `days I had no guardian while disabled`
        `close relationship while disabled`         IS `close relationship during disability`
        `close relationship has ceased`             IS `has that relationship ended`
        `close relationship ceased on`              IS `day it ended`)

@export My injury was suffered at or just after my birth, before 15 November 2005: is my action barred (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 7)? It cannot be brought after 15 November 2011, or once the period under the old law expired, unless a court extends the time under Part 3 (counting from 15 November 2005).
GIVEN `was it at my birth` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the personal injury was incurred while your mother gave birth to you, or immediately after and arising from the birth (natural or by a medical procedure)
      `did it accrue before 15 November 2005` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the cause of action accrued before 15 November 2005
      `has the old period expired` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the limitation period that would have applied under the law before 15 November 2005 has expired
      `day I would commence` IS A DATE @desc The day the writ or other originating application would be issued
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my birth injury action barred` MEANS
    `s 7(2) -- the childbirth action cannot be commenced` `was it at my birth` `did it accrue before 15 November 2005` `has the old period expired` `day I would commence`

§§ `More time from the court (arises if your limitation period has run out)`

@export Can the court give me more time because the other side's fraud or improper conduct stopped me suing, and up to when (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 38)? Up to 3 years from when you ought reasonably to have started; not for defamation. You must prove the court should extend (s 79(3)); it weighs a fair trial and prejudice to the defendant (s 44).
GIVEN `is the court satisfied of fraud` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that your failure to start the action was caused by fraudulent or other improper conduct of the defendant, or of someone the defendant is vicariously liable for (the court's judgment)
      `day I ought to have started` IS A DATE @desc The day by which you ought reasonably to have started the action
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`Can the court extend my time for fraud` MEANS
    `s 38 -- extension for fraud or improper conduct` `is the court satisfied of fraud` `day I ought to have started`

@export Can the court give me more time for my personal injury or death claim because I did not know its cause, who caused it, or who they were, and up to when (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 39)? Up to 3 years from when you knew, or ought reasonably to have known, all three. The court weighs a fair trial and prejudice to the defendant (s 44).
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for (only damages for a personal injury, or a Fatal Accidents Act 1959 claim for a death, can be extended under this section)
      `was I aware of the cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when the limitation period expired, you (or your guardian, if you were under 18 or have a mental disability) were aware of the physical cause of the injury or death
      `was I aware someone caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, then, you were aware that the injury or death was attributable to someone's conduct
      `did I know who they were` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, then, you knew who that person was
      `did I enquire` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you had made reasonable enquiries to find out who that person was
      `day I knew all three` IS A DATE @desc The day you became aware, or ought reasonably to have become aware, of the cause, that someone's conduct caused it, and who they were
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`Can the court extend my time for a personal injury claim` MEANS
    `s 39 -- extension for personal injury or death` `what kind of action` `was I aware of the cause` `was I aware someone caused it` `did I know who they were` `did I enquire` `day I knew all three`

@export I was under 18 when my claim accrued and had a guardian who did not sue: can the court give me more time, and up to when (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 41)? Up to when you turn 21, if the court is satisfied it was unreasonable for your guardian not to sue in time; not for defamation.
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued
      `is the court satisfied about my guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that it was unreasonable for your guardian not to start the action within the limitation period (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`Can the court extend my time because I was under 18` MEANS
    `s 41 -- extension for a person under 18 with a guardian` `my date of birth` `day it accrued` `is the court satisfied about my guardian`

@export I have had a mental disability since my claim accrued, and my guardian did not sue: can the court give me more time, and up to when (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 42)? Up to 12 years from when the claim accrued, if the court is satisfied it was unreasonable for your guardian not to sue in time; not for defamation.
GIVEN `have I had a mental disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether at any time since the cause of action accrued you have had a mental disability that left you unable to make reasonable judgments about yourself or your property
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued
      `is the court satisfied about my guardian` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court is satisfied that it was unreasonable for your guardian not to start the action within the limitation period (the court's judgment)
GIVETH A `Court extension`
`Can the court extend my time because of my mental disability` MEANS
    `s 42 -- extension for a person with a mental disability with a guardian` `have I had a mental disability` `day it accrued` `is the court satisfied about my guardian`

@export In a dispute about my limitation period, who has to prove it (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 79)? The defendant must prove the time has run out; you must prove that time without a guardian does not count, and that the court should extend the time.
GIVEN `which issue` IS AN `Issue to prove` @desc What has to be proved: that the limitation period has expired; that time without a guardian (while under 18, or during a mental disability) does not count; or that the court should extend the time
GIVETH A `Who must prove it`
`Who has to prove it` MEANS
    `s 79 -- who must prove it` `which issue`

§§ `More time by agreement or confirmation`

@export Does a term of my agreement that extends or shortens my limitation period have effect (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 45)? Such agreements are allowed, but a term that tries to exclude the extensions for a close relationship (ss 33, 36) or for fraud (s 38), or to extinguish rather than bar a right, has no effect.
GIVEN `does it exclude those sections` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the term tries to exclude section 33, 36 or 38, or to extinguish (rather than merely bar) a right or title to land
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Does my agreed time limit have effect` MEANS
    `s 45 -- the agreed term has effect` `does it exclude those sections`

@export Did the other side's acknowledgment of my claim, or a payment, give me a fresh limitation period, and to when (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) ss 46 to 50)? It must come after the claim accrued and before the time ran out, and an acknowledgment must be in writing and signed by its maker.
GIVEN `what kind of action` IS A `Kind of action` @desc What the action is for (as in the time limit question)
      `day it accrued` IS A DATE @desc The day the cause of action accrued
      `what did they give` IS A `Kind of confirmation` @desc What was given: a written acknowledgment of your right signed by its maker; an acknowledgment that is not in writing or not signed; a payment to you made in circumstances consistent with acknowledging your right; or nothing
      `does it bind the person I would sue` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made by the person you would sue, or by someone whose confirmation binds them (the person they inherited the liability from, an earlier executor or trustee of the same estate or trust)
      `day it was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the acknowledgment or payment was made
GIVETH A `Confirmation effect`
`Did a confirmation give me more time` MEANS
    `ss 46-50 -- what the confirmation does` `what kind of action` `day it accrued` `what did they give` `does it bind the person I would sue` `day it was given`

§§ `Answering a claim (arises if you are sued and counterclaim)`

@export I am being sued and want to counterclaim: on what day is my counterclaim taken to have been started, for my limitation period (Limitation Act 2005 (WA) s 81)? Against the plaintiff, the day you became a party; against someone you join, the day they were joined.
GIVEN `is it only a defence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the counterclaim is solely a way of defending the claim (for example a set-off that only reduces what you owe), not a claim of your own
      `against whom` IS A `Counterclaim against` @desc Whom the counterclaim is against: the plaintiff who sued you, or another person you joined to the counterclaim
      `day I became a party` IS A DATE @desc The day you became a party to the action
      `day they were joined` IS A DATE @desc The day the other person was joined to the counterclaim (any date if not applicable)
GIVETH A `Counterclaim commencement`
`When is my counterclaim taken to have started` MEANS
    `s 81 -- when my counterclaim is taken to commence` `is it only a defence` `against whom` `day I became a party` `day they were joined`
